emit("## Findings (12 October 2026)")
emit("")
emit("1. **Why SmeltingFurnace, Prospector, OreChute and CraftBench stayed part-built.** Their ids are")
emit("   correct: every machine piece id matches `assets/uploaded-machines-tld1.json` or")
emit("   `assets/uploaded-machines-rocks.json`, and each has a MeshTemplates file. The cause was timing plus a")
emit("   missing swap. MiningService builds those four at server start; the `machines` group is last in")
emit("   MeshManifest, so its meshes were still queued behind about 500 others. `MiningArt` called")
emit('   `MachineSkin.Prepare` outside `MeshKit.Attempt`, so the miss was final (and logged as "did not')
emit('   load" although the load was only pending). MiningArt now builds the part-built machine first and')
emit("   swaps the mesh in when it lands (`MeshKit.Attempt`), like every other builder.")
emit("2. **Same gap remains for plot machines** (sawmills, planers, chop saw, belts, Sky Bin via MachineArt):")
emit("   a machine built before its meshes are cached stays part-built until its model is rebuilt (rejoin or")
emit("   re-place). MachineSkin now logs `was still loading` instead of `did not load` in that case. A real fix")
emit("   needs PlotService to re-dress; not done here (touches plot item registration).")
emit("3. **Store card images** (`StoreData` image ids 91282142796474, 79037897236948, 71028498113750) are")
emit("   possibly Decal ids, which an ImageLabel cannot load by rbxassetid. They now go through `StoreArt`")
